title: Cabinet Reshuffle
subtitle: Reopen every portfolio—or leave the cabinet untouched.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and ministry_count >= 1 and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_cabinet_reshuffle_timer <= 0
on-arrival: poland_cabinet_reshuffle_timer = 6
card-image: img/poland/cards/reshuffle.webp

= Cabinet Reshuffle

[? if government_party = "pis": Six months inside Morawiecki's government have
changed the price of every office. Kaczyński still refuses to discuss the
coercive ministries, but delivery failures have reopened the social and
economic portfolios. Lewica now knows which nameplates carry authority and
which merely carry blame.?]
[? if government_party != "pis": Six months of government have changed the
price of every office. KO wants its senior ministries back, PSL wants
Agriculture and Defence treated as natural property, and Lewica now knows
which nameplates carry authority.?]

A reshuffle can reopen the whole cabinet table; even declining it consumes the
action used to conduct the cabinet review.

- @renegotiate
- @delivery_letters
- @keep

@renegotiate
title: Reopen the whole portfolio table
subtitle: Spend this month's action and conduct a live cabinet negotiation.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; ministry_allocation_mode = "reshuffle"; ministry_return_mode = "card_finish"; ministry_reshuffle_previous_count = ministry_count; news_headline = "Lewica reopens every cabinet portfolio for negotiation"
go-to: poland_ministries


@delivery_letters
title: Keep the ministers and impose public delivery letters
subtitle: Spend this month's action on accountability without trading offices.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; government_delivery += 2; public_trust += 2; government_coalition_dissent += 1; news_headline = "Cabinet ministers receive public one-hundred-day delivery letters"

No office changes hands. Each minister receives a short list of dated
commitments, allowing the next reshuffle argument to begin with a record
rather than rumours passed between coalition leaders.

- #poland_card_finish


@keep
title: Keep the cabinet exactly as it is
subtitle: No office, resource or budget changes; the partners read the stability as a decision rather than an absence.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; government_coalition_dissent -= 2; party_unity += 1; ko_relation += 1 if government_party != "pis"; psl_relation += 1 if government_party != "pis"; pis_relation += 1 if government_party = "pis"; last_card_objection = 0; news_headline = "The cabinet review closes without a change of office"

The review ends without a reshuffle. Every minister keeps the portfolio they
were promised at formation, which is the one thing the coalition has never had
to argue about this quarter.

Stability is not nothing: the partners who expected a demand and did not get
one become fractionally easier to deal with in the next fight.

- #poland_card_finish
